On May 1, 1:17 pm, Mylar <mylar...@yahoo.com> wrote:

> 5. I get stuck with useless extra weapon artifacts. Can I give them to
> my pets? What silly things can my pets do to cause them to end up
> destroyed, if any.

Make sure your pet is a kind that can wield weapons, and that they're
not already wielding one. If they are, you may try applying a bullwhip
to relieve them of it.

Note that the only time thus far I have given artifacts to pets, one
pet got disintegrated in Gehennom and the other died on the Plane of
Fire - an Angel and an Aleax with Sunsword and Excalibur, respectively
- I was dual-weaponing Frost Brand with a silver saber myself. *Don't*
give a pet Vorpal Blade or the Tsurugi! You don't want to get
decapitated or bisected if they get confused, or killed, leaving it
lying around for another intelligent monster to pick up.

> 6. When gathering junk to polypile, I generally don't bother ID'ing
> it. If one of those silver sabers is the unidentified greyswandir (sp)
> and I poly it, will it be affected? Should I be ID'ing trash to make
> sure I don't poly artifacts out of existance?

Artifact weapons are always pre-IDd (for name, not enchantment or B/U/
C status) as far as I know, and should have a very high resistance to
being polymorphed should you still accidentally drop it on the pile.
But I'm not positive about that latter point, so be careful.

> 8. Why does noone use yellow dragon scale? MR comes from alot of
> artifacts and if you are not a dual wield class, why not use a shield
> of relfection... at that point the only intrinsic you are missing is
> acid. I would think Yellow dragon scale would be as commonly used as
> grey... Silver I see some use for in the case of dual wielders or
> casters who want their neck free for lifesaving, but I see people
> getting grey alot and I just don't see the need.

I've never found acid damage to be enough worry to even consider using
that color scale mail. I've always worn silver or gray. I never trust
leaving MR to a quest artifact as it can be stolen, and I haven't
burned a single amulet of lifesaving in my last eight ascensions so
I'm now preferring to save that spot for reflection if I choose gray
scales over silver. I don't like the shield penalty for spellcasting.

Though the one time I had a *pet* yellow dragon, he proved quite handy
as he could kill and eat cockatrices. Some would find this a downside
but I normally prefer to avoid wielding rubber chickens, myself, and
don't want to leave them lying around for intelligent monsters to use
against me.

> 11. Grave digging penalties are outlined clearly, is there any reason
> TO gravedig? I only ever see to end up with player monster corpses or
> zombies trying to chew on me.

Occasionally you might dig up one or more items. I tend to find much
more in the chests and boxes in graveyards than in the graves
themselves though.

> 12. Player monster corpses. I spent a good bit of time using turn
> undead to revive and then kill Eidolas and CDI player corpses over and
> over when I got into the valley, I was expecting them to drop nice
> class weighted loot, they didn't. Is there any point to these other
> then the fun of watching my pet dragons chew on the leaderboard?

The names are from the high score list but these corpses aren't like
ghosts from bones levels; they won't be carrying their namesake's
inventory.

